{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DESIGN DECISION (operator-ratified, grounded in OSS research): adopt SINGLE-SOURCING — remove the CLI --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread flags from _build-and-test.yml's two shared-tier lanes and let [tool.pytest.ini_options] govern. Precedent: pytest-timeout precedence is CLI > env > ini (get_env_settings in pytest_timeout.py), so a CI CLI flag permanently shadows any ini change carried in a patchset — the trusted-main workflow-file mechanism this ticket documents; scikit-learn, pandas and numpy pass no --timeout on their CI command lines. The previously drafted conftest-floor approach (branch preserve/timeout-floor-hardening, commit b38bf9a4748) is REJECTED: pytest-timeout resolves config._env_timeout at session start read-only, so a conftest floor has no supported hook point and no OSS precedent. That branch is mined for reusable test assets only (its parity-contract rewrites and lane-flag removals); its floor mechanism (tests/_timeout_floor.py, the conftest hook, the docs floor section) does not land. Effective budgets before/after: lanes ran at CLI --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread; the ini already carries timeout=300, timeout_method=thread — identical values, so removing the flags changes no effective budget, it only moves authority to the ini so a future patchset's ini change is exercised by its own Verified run. The branch will be deleted after mining (it exists locally only; no origin ref)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787449543378001001,"uuid":"968da90d-da09-435c-ac1b-9a7e49ba0b28"}